`GET /api/v1/ai/agents` returned 404 because `buildAgentRoutes()` was never called. The Studio AI Chat panel consequently only showed "General Chat", with `data_chat` and `metadata_assistant` agents invisible.

## Root Cause

There were two root causes:

### 1. Kernel bootstrap timing (primary) — `packages/core/src/kernel.ts`

`ObjectKernel.bootstrap()` only injected in-memory fallbacks for 'core' services (including `'metadata'`) inside `validateSystemRequirements()`, which runs **after** all plugin `start()` methods complete. This meant `ctx.getService('metadata')` always threw during `AIServicePlugin.start()` when no explicit `MetadataPlugin` was loaded — making `metadataService` always `undefined`, so neither agent registration nor `buildAgentRoutes()` could ever execute.

### 2. Shadowed variable (secondary) — `packages/services/service-ai/src/plugin.ts`

A redundant second `ctx.getService<IMetadataService>('metadata')` call redeclared `metadataService` as `const`, shadowing the outer `let metadataService`. Even if the outer variable had been set, the empty `catch` on this inner call would silently skip `buildAgentRoutes()`.

## Changes

### `packages/core/src/kernel.ts`
- Added `preInjectCoreFallbacks()` private method that injects in-memory fallbacks for all `'core'`-criticality services (metadata, cache, queue, i18n, job) that weren't registered by Phase 1
- Call `preInjectCoreFallbacks()` between Phase 1 (init) and Phase 2 (start) so `ctx.getService('metadata')` always succeeds during any plugin's `start()`

### `packages/services/service-ai/src/plugin.ts`
- Drop the redundant `try/catch` re-fetch block entirely
- Reuse the already-resolved outer `metadataService` variable with a plain `if` check

```ts
// Before — shadows outer variable, fails silently
try {
  const metadataService = ctx.getService<IMetadataService>('metadata'); // ← new const, shadows outer let
  if (metadataService) {
    routes.push(...buildAgentRoutes(this.service, new AgentRuntime(metadataService), ctx.logger));
  }
} catch {
  ctx.logger.debug('[AI] Metadata service not available, skipping agent routes');
}

// After — reuses the already-resolved outer variable
if (metadataService) {
  const agentRuntime = new AgentRuntime(metadataService);
  const agentRoutes = buildAgentRoutes(this.service, agentRuntime, ctx.logger);
  routes.push(...agentRoutes);
  ctx.logger.info(`[AI] Agent routes registered (${agentRoutes.length} routes)`);
} else {
  ctx.logger.debug('[AI] Metadata service not available, skipping agent routes');
}
```

### `packages/runtime/src/dispatcher-plugin.ts`
- Extract `mountRouteOnServer()` helper — eliminates duplicated per-route handler construction
- Add fallback at end of `start()`: if `AIServicePlugin.start()` fires `ai:routes` before `DispatcherPlugin` registers its hook listener (start-order edge case), recover from `kernel.__aiRoutes` cache and mount any missed routes
- Use `String(v)` instead of `as string` cast for header values

