## Problem

When running `pnpm dev`, the AI Chat panel in Studio only shows "General Chat" — the agent selector dropdown does not display `data_chat` or `metadata_assistant` agents. The root cause is that `GET /api/v1/ai/agents` returns 404 because agent routes are never registered on the HTTP server.

### Diagnosis

`curl -s http://localhost:3001/api/v1/ai/chat -X POST -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"hello"}],"stream":false}'` works fine, confirming the AI service itself is running. But `curl http://localhost:3001/api/v1/ai/agents` returns 404.

### Root Cause

In `packages/services/service-ai/src/plugin.ts`, the `start()` method has TWO separate `ctx.getService('metadata')` calls:

1. **Line ~250-255** — Successfully obtains the metadata service and uses it to register agents and tools:
```typescript
let metadataService: IMetadataService | undefined;
try {
  metadataService = ctx.getService<IMetadataService>('metadata');
} catch {
  ctx.logger.debug('[AI] Metadata service not available');
}
```

2. **Line ~310-320** — Attempts to get the metadata service AGAIN with a new `const` declaration (shadowing the outer variable), and this second call fails silently:
```typescript
// Build agent routes if metadata service is available
try {
  const metadataService = ctx.getService<IMetadataService>('metadata'); // ← redundant re-fetch, shadows outer variable
  if (metadataService) {
    const agentRuntime = new AgentRuntime(metadataService);
    const agentRoutes = buildAgentRoutes(this.service, agentRuntime, ctx.logger);
    routes.push(...agentRoutes);
  }
} catch {
  ctx.logger.debug('[AI] Metadata service not available, skipping agent routes'); // ← silently swallows the real error
}
```

The second `ctx.getService('metadata')` call can fail due to async factory resolution issues or service state inconsistency, while the first call succeeds. Because the failure is caught by an empty `catch` block, `buildAgentRoutes()` is never called, and the `routes` array only contains routes from `buildAIRoutes()` (chat, complete, models, conversations) but NOT the agent routes (`GET /api/v1/ai/agents`, `POST /api/v1/ai/agents/:agentName/chat`).

When `ctx.trigger('ai:routes', routes)` fires, only the non-agent routes get registered on the Hono HTTP server via the DispatcherPlugin's `ai:routes` hook listener. This explains why `/api/v1/ai/chat` works but `/api/v1/ai/agents` returns 404.

